      "@id": "kt:agentic-workflow",
      "@type": "kto:Technique",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Agentic workflow",
      "skos:definition": "A way of building LLM applications in which several model calls and tool calls are orchestrated along code paths the developer defines in advance, such as chains, routers, parallel branches, orchestrator–worker splits and generate–critique loops, rather than leaving the overall control flow to the model.",
